  "source": {
    "algorithm_version_file": "32a74b5",
    "commit": "83851dbbe129d30522f2934dd94144e44daa154b",
    "commit_body": "CONVICTION / REJECTION now blend toward a direction-aware target\n(0 or 100) weighted by magnitude \u00d7 vol_boost (cap 0.60), replacing\nthe asymmetric `50 + (score-50) \u00d7 (1 + deviation)` multiplicative\nformula. The old path amplified distance from 50 regardless of\nvol direction, so a bullish volume signal on a below-50 score\npushed the score FURTHER below 50, pinning many stocks at 0.\n\n47/47 zero-score rows in the active version had bullish volume\n(vol_raw>50); 95% of scores <5 and 83% of scores <10 had\ncontra-directional volume \u2014 a systematic sign-inversion bug.\n\nSimulated v4a (blend cap 0.60) on 150-stock random sample \u00d7 2y:\n  70+ WR 65.7% \u2192 67.5%, Cap30 0.176 \u2192 0.207 (N=2283)\n  75+ WR 64.2% \u2192 67.2%, Cap30 0.199 \u2192 0.240 (N=1072)\n  80+ WR 61.1% \u2192 63.7%, Cap30 0.237 \u2192 0.191 (N=370)\n  85+ WR 65.6% \u2192 69.0%, Cap30 0.391 \u2192 0.412 (N=80)\n  <25 near-neutral (N=1827)\n  Zero clustering eliminated.\n\nTHIN_AIR keeps original multiplicative dampening (vol_mult<1 pulls\ntoward 50 which is correct \"no conviction\").\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "83851dbb",
    "commit_subject": "Fix zero-score clustering from asymmetric volume amplification",
    "mode": "git_ref",
